Package: rbr.multiclass.genes
Title: A Bayesian Feature Selection Method for Multiclass Classification with
    Application to Cancer Gene Expression Data
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Maher", "Emarly", email = "maheremarly1@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ayman", "Alzaatreh", role = "aut"),
    person("Luai", "Al-Labadi", role = "aut"))
Description: Code for the paper of the same name (preprint,
    doi:10.21203/rs.3.rs-9106857/v1). Extends the relative belief ratio filter
    from two classes to k, scoring each gene by the evidence against equality of
    its class-conditional means, and benchmarks it against information gain,
    symmetric uncertainty, mRMR and ReliefF on cancer microarray datasets
    with four classifiers under five-fold cross-validation. This is a research
    project, not an installable package: the modules in R/ are sourced by the
    entry points in scripts/.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    abind,
    caret,
    class,
    CORElearn,
    dplyr,
    e1071,
    FSelector,
    glmnet,
    ggplot2,
    gridExtra,
    openxlsx,
    praznik,
    randomForest,
    reshape2,
    scales,
    yaml
Additional_repositories: https://github.com/ramhiser/datamicroarray
SystemRequirements: Java (>= 8), required by FSelector via RWeka. The
    datamicroarray package is not on CRAN; install it with
    remotes::install_github("ramhiser/datamicroarray").
